<title>USA: US banks free reserves $1.004 bln Nov 20 two weeks.</title>
<headline>US banks free reserves $1.004 bln Nov 20 two weeks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $1.004 billion per day in the two weeks ended November 20, versus revised free reserves of $842 million in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $108 million versus $154 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
